  "notes": [
   "Breadboard row letters: the picture's top half (rows j-f) is mapped to catalogue bank 't' (rows a-e, image j->a ... f->e) and the bottom half (rows e-a) to bank 'b' (rows f-j, image e->f ... a->j). Only strip membership matters.",
   "Rail naming assumed: top '-' row = tn, top '+' row = tp, bottom '-' row = bn, bottom '+' row = bp. Rail hole numbers are approximate positions from the picture.",
   "Pushbutton straddles the centre gap in columns 4 and 6: column 4 (side 1) carries pin 2 and the 10k pull-down to ground, column 6 (side 2) is tied to 5V.",
   "Photoresistor spans columns 10 and 14: column 10 goes to A0 and a 10k resistor to ground, column 14 goes to 5V.",
   "LED anode (18t) is fed from pin 9 via the 220 ohm resistor (15t to 18t); cathode (19t) goes to the top ground rail via a black wire.",
   "Both ground rails are linked by a black wire and both 5V rails by a red wire at the right edge. Arduino GND.2 was chosen for the ground wire.",
   "The text says 'analog input 2' but the picture, schematic and code use A0."
  ]
